From fc49b63b427dacbd59491090754436a801101533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Charliechen114514 <725610365@qq.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 01:04:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: rockchip: keep RK3588 PD_GMAC always-on

genpd_power_off_unused() (late initcall) powers RK3588 PD_GMAC off because
stmmac holds no runtime-PM usage on it. On this silicon, any later access
to a powered-off GMAC wedges the SoC bus with no error return: the AXI
fabric stalls, vblank and other IRQs starve, PMIC SPI (RK806) transfers
time out (-110), and whichever CPU touches a starved path hard-locks.

Vendor BSP dodges the same behavior with the pm_domains.always_on=1 +
clk_gate.always_on=1 module parameters (rk3588-nvr-demo bootargs); do it
domain-scoped instead.

Board evidence: rk-forge logs rk3588/nfs/{1..6}.txt (2026-10-31/11-01).
---
 drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
index 490bbb1d1..d9e39963c 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/rockchip/pm-domains.c
@@ -1092,6 +1092,22 @@ static int rockchip_pm_domain_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto err_out;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * RK3588 PD_GMAC must stay on: genpd_power_off_unused() powers it off
+	 * during late init because stmmac holds no runtime-PM usage, and any
+	 * later GMAC access then wedges the SoC bus with no error return
+	 * (fabric-wide stall: IRQ starvation, hard lockups, PMIC SPI -110).
+	 * Vendor BSP dodges the same silicon behavior with the
+	 * pm_domains.always_on module parameter; scope it to this domain.
+	 */
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(np, "rockchip,rk3588-power-controller")) {
+		struct generic_pm_domain *gmac_pd =
+			pmu->genpd_data.domains[RK3588_PD_GMAC];
+
+		if (gmac_pd)
+			gmac_pd->flags |= GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON;
+	}
+
 	error = of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(np, &pmu->genpd_data);
 	if (error) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to add provider: %d\n", error);
-- 
2.43.0

